github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6240#issuecomment-5534637237","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUMmgW88AAAABSeQiVw","author":{"login":"qodo-code-review"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"<h3>Code Review by Qodo</h3>\n\n<code>🐞 Bugs (1)</code>  <code>📘 Rule violations (0)</code>  <code>📜 Skill insights (0)</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/High-634FD1?style=flat-square\" height=\"20px\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  1.  Legacy subclasses fail dispatch <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>≡ Correctness</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>Removing the subclass adapters makes Flask 3.1-style overrides such as <b><i>dispatch_request(self)</i></b>\n>receive an unexpected <b><i>AppContext</i></b>, causing request dispatch or teardown to fail with <b><i>TypeError</i></b>.\n>The deleted warning explicitly promised support until Flask 4.0, while this branch is the unreleased\n>3.2 release.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[src/flask/app.py[L308-309]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6240/files#diff-d3e0349504081bb501c611b3954be364188a4cf442056181272e27e830ae446eL308-L309)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>-                setattr(cls, method.__name__, remove_ctx(method))\n>-                setattr(Flask, method.__name__, add_ctx(base_method))\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The WSGI entry point passes <b><i>ctx</i></b> to <b><i>full_dispatch_request</i></b> and <b><i>handle_exception</i></b>; those methods\n>then pass it to overridable dispatch, preprocessing, finalization, logging, and response hooks. With\n>the deleted adapters, any existing override that accepts only the previously public arguments\n>receives one extra positional argument; the changelog identifies this branch as unreleased Flask 3.2\n>rather than the Flask 4.0 removal boundary named by the deleted deprecation warning.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[src/flask/app.py[1508-1516]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/2ac81868274b34c9a4a2788d07ead14cc093e970/src/flask/app.py/#L1508-L1516)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/app.py[908-935]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/2ac81868274b34c9a4a2788d07ead14cc093e970/src/flask/app.py/#L908-L935)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/app.py[813-864]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/2ac81868274b34c9a4a2788d07ead14cc093e970/src/flask/app.py/#L813-L864)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/app.py[1282-1334]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/2ac81868274b34c9a4a2788d07ead14cc093e970/src/flask/app.py/#L1282-L1334)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/app.py[1336-1395]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/2ac81868274b34c9a4a2788d07ead14cc093e970/src/flask/app.py/#L1336-L1395)</code>\n> <code>[CHANGES.rst[1-4]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/2ac81868274b34c9a4a2788d07ead14cc093e970/CHANGES.rst/#L1-L4)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>Removing `Flask.__init_subclass__` and its argument adapters breaks subclasses overriding lifecycle methods with their Flask 3.1 signatures. Internal dispatch now passes an `AppContext` unconditionally, so these overrides raise `TypeError` despite the compatibility period previously extending through Flask 3.x.\n>\n>## Issue Context\n>Restore compatibility without globally mutating methods on `Flask`, or retain the released method signatures and obtain the active context internally. Add regression tests covering old-signature dispatch, error handling, response processing, and teardown overrides, including overrides that call `super()`.\n>\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- src/flask/app.py[79-79]\n>- src/flask/app.py[882-935]\n>- src/flask/app.py[1282-1370]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<!-- qodo-context:start -->\n<details><summary><strong>Context sources</strong></summary>\n\n<div>Review mode: <code>⚖️ Balanced</code>: This removes compatibility machinery for subclass method signatures in Flask’s central dispatch path, creating meaningful public-behavior and backward-compatibility risk despite being localized to one file.</div>\n<!-- qodo-context:end -->\n</details>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n\n<!-- qodo-daily-tip:start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Tip of the day</strong></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n<pre>💡 Did you know, you can route each action level your way: inline, summary, both, or drop</pre>\n\n<a href=\"https://docs.qodo.ai/tips-and-tricks\">More tips ↗</a> | <a href=\"https://app.qodo.ai/configurations?tab=display-preferences\">Customize Qodo ↗</a> | <a href=\"https://docs.qodo.ai\">Qodo docs ↗</a>\n\n</details>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n<!-- qodo-daily-tip:end -->\n\n\n<!-- https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/commit/2ac81868274b34c9a4a2788d07ead14cc093e970 -->\n\n<a href=\"https://www.qodo.ai\"><img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/qodo-logo.svg\" width=\"80\" alt=\"Qodo Logo\"></a>","createdAt":"2026-09-04T02:07:42Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https